Think: Good, the CSV file is created with the format: line_number+Bob, action, stock_index, count. Now I need to aggregate this data by stock index to produce "bob_stock_summary.csv" containing per-index totals and flags: total_bought, total_sold, net_count, ever_bought (true/false), and ever_sold (true/false). This is complex, so I'll use awk to process the data.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F',' '
{
    stock = $3
    action = $2
    count = $4

    if (action == "Purchase") {
        bought[stock] += count
        ever_bought[stock] = "true"
    } else if (action == "Sell") {
        sold[stock] += count
        ever_sold[stock] = "true"
    }
}
END {
    # Get all unique stock indices
    for (stock in bought) stocks[stock] = 1
    for (stock in sold) stocks[stock] = 1

    for (stock in stocks) {
        total_bought = (bought[stock] ? bought[stock] : 0)
        total_sold = (sold[stock] ? sold[stock] : 0)
        net_count = total_bought - total_sold
        eb = (ever_bought[stock] ? "true" : "false")
        es = (ever_sold[stock] ? "true" : "false")

        print stock "," total_bought "," total_sold "," net_count "," eb "," es
    }
}' temp_stock_analysis/bob_counts.csv > temp_stock_analysis/bob_stock_summary.csv
```
